WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:04.587
There is a universe of small molecules hidden in plain sight.

00:00:04.587 --> 00:00:07.882
The small molecules are beautiful structures

00:00:07.882 --> 00:00:11.428
and it allows us to think about really the beauty of nature.

00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:14.305
My name is Jason Crawford and I'm a chemical biologist.

00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:20.520
I'm the director of the Institute of Biomolecular Design and Discovery
on the West Campus.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.024
And our mission is to employ chemical biology

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:26.651
to solve problems in human health.

00:00:26.651 --> 00:00:32.365
Chemical biology, by definition, is interdisciplinary.

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:37.954
The West Campus, its mission is to promote interdisciplinary science.

00:00:37.954 --> 00:00:41.416
And I just love getting people with different mindsets

00:00:41.416 --> 00:00:45.879
all in the same room and thinking about a common goal.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:50.633
We focus on the basic science of cellular physiology,

00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:54.637
how the molecules regulate cellular processes.

00:00:54.637 --> 00:01:00.935
And what is fascinating is that if you look at any cell,
whether it's a microbe or a human tissue,

00:01:00.935 --> 00:01:06.649
greater than 90% of the molecules in those cells remain unknown.

00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:10.695
So a big part of our group is to parse apart the junk

00:01:10.695 --> 00:01:14.574
from the molecules that represent novel metabolic pathways.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:20.038
And if you can decode a novel metabolic
pathway, this opens completely new doors

00:01:20.038 --> 00:01:25.502
for a wide variety of directions,
including preclinical drug development.

00:01:25.502 --> 00:01:28.671
So one of the guiding principles of our lab

00:01:28.671 --> 00:01:32.926
is to decode these metabolic pathways and understand

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:39.224
how microbes can alter human physiology.

00:01:39.224 --> 00:01:43.812
We look at specific responses like how do the microbes
regulate inflammation

00:01:43.812 --> 00:01:49.526
and how do they damage your DNA,
which can be linked to colorectal cancer?

00:01:49.526 --> 00:01:54.489
I try to encourage my students to tackle problems from multiple angles.

00:01:54.489 --> 00:01:57.492
Of course, give them feedback as we go.

00:01:57.492 --> 00:02:00.495
But really, my job
is to help them with the big picture

00:02:00.495 --> 00:02:03.957
and push goals at a thematic level.

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:08.837
Chemical biology at Yale spans
Yale's West Campus

00:02:08.837 --> 00:02:13.133
The Faculty of Arts and Sciences on the main campus
and the Yale School of Medicine.

00:02:13.174 --> 00:02:17.679
We try to collaborate to promote the best science at Yale.

00:02:17.679 --> 00:02:20.515
I'm just truly fascinated by this area

00:02:20.515 --> 00:02:24.435
and I can't imagine doing anything else with my career.

